From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:32:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(weekly): last week's food, training and overall marks on
 Today

Once a week is over (Monday to Sunday), Claude reviews it as a whole: food
(quality, protein, regularity, portions and the energy balance against the
goals), training (volume, frequency, balance, intensity against recovery,
rest, consistency) and overall, each 0-10 with one reason, plus the one thing
to focus on this week. It reads the week's meals with their marks, the burn per
day, every workout (strap, imports, logged) with its exercises and session
mark and, under the coach's consent, profile, scale, goals and the strap's
daily table. A week with fewer than three days of meals and no workout is not
reviewed; an area with too little to judge shows a dash.

'Tu semana' sits under the Today food card as one line of three marks; a tap
opens the reasons and the focus. The coach gets a LAST WEEK REVIEW line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
